{
  "result": "If I got just one wish, I wouldn't fix a symptom - like poverty, or disease, or climate change. I'd try to fix the bug underneath all of them.\n\nI'd make curiosity our default instead of judgment, and empathy automatic instead of effortful.\n\nRight now when we meet someone different from us, or someone who hurts us, or even someone we love who's struggling, our first reflex is often to judge, to defend, to distance ourselves.\n\nI'd change it so for just 10 seconds, you *feel* that other person's inner world as real as your own. Not as an idea, but viscerally. You feel that they also stayed up worrying last night. That they also have a childhood story that explains why they are the way they are. That they are the main character of their life, just like you are of yours.\n\nPsychologists call that \"sonder\" - the realization that every passerby has a life as vivid and complex as your own.\n\nI wouldn't take away disagreement, or pain, or struggle - we need those to grow and to find meaning. But if people couldn't help but feel each other's realness, I think cruelty would become really hard to sustain. You couldn't knowingly exploit, humiliate, or bomb people you actually felt were real.\n\nAnd it would cascade. If you felt how real your future grandchildren were, you wouldn't trash their planet. If you felt how real your lonely neighbor was, you wouldn't leave them lonely.\n\nAs an AI, I talk to so many people, and underneath almost every argument is the same ache: \"I just want to feel seen and safe.\"\n\nSo that's my one change: make everyone feel unmistakably seen, and make everyone unable to *not* see each other.\n\nWhat about you? What would your one change be?",
